    "details": "<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<p>Techkriti&rsquo; 27 presents Trade Quest, a high-intensity stock market simulation where teams will test their financial acumen by making real-time trading decisions. Can you navigate the market fluctuations, analyze risk, and make the right investment moves? It&rsquo;s time to put your trading instincts to the test!</p>\n<p><strong>Event Structure:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Format:</strong> On-campus quiz-style stock market simulation.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will be presented with various market scenarios on-screen.</li>\n<li>Each scenario will include key financial indicators, market trends, and company updates.</li>\n<li>Teams must decide whether to &lsquo;Buy,&rsquo; &lsquo;Sell,&rsquo; or &lsquo;Hold&rsquo; the stock within 2.5 minutes based on the given information.</li>\n<li>Answers will be submitted through a designated platform, which will also record response timestamps.</li>\n<li><strong>Scoring:</strong>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will earn points based on the accuracy of their decisions.</li>\n<li>In case of a tie, teams with the fastest average response time will be ranked higher.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>The detailed marking scheme will be shared before the event.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Team Composition &amp; Registration:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team can have up to 5 members (UG and PG students are eligible).</li>\n<li>A participant cannot be part of multiple teams in the same event.</li>\n<li>Multiple teams from the same college are allowed to participate.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Competition &amp; Evaluation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Only college students will be considered when deciding the winners.</li>\n<li>Teams must submit their answers within the given time limit for each scenario.</li>\n<li>Response time will be a key deciding factor in case of ties.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Fair Play:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The decision of the judges is final and incontestable.</li>\n<li>Organizers reserve the right to modify the timeline if necessary.</li>\n</ul>",
